{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"linen-contrived-wisent","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Update canonical documentation to the new force governance model (operator ruling 2026-08-18): force is allowed through ANY command surface (lib, CLI, MCP); auditability comes from the ABSENCE of a signed attestation (a force op produces no attestation / closed-without-signature), and projects that want to prevent force from circumventing protections check for certification in their CI pipeline.\n\nSTALE TEXT TO FIX:\n- AGENTS.md: \"--force ... is CLI-only and not exposed over MCP\" — rewrite to force-everywhere + absent-attestation audit + CI-certification enforcement. (Copilot/Claude bridge files import AGENTS.md, so one edit propagates.)\n- MCP tool docstrings in src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py that assert \"intentionally NO force bypass over MCP\" (transition_ticket, claim_ticket) — rewrite to match the new capability.\n- Any docs/*.md describing force as CLI/lib-only.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n- AGENTS.md + MCP docstrings state force is available on all surfaces and describe the absent-attestation audit model + CI-certification enforcement option.\n- No remaining doc claims force is CLI-only / unavailable over MCP.\n- Consistent with the MCP-parity sibling (the code actually exposes force before/with this doc change).","id":"d8c1-e75e-77d8-4c00","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Docs: force allowed on all surfaces, audited by absent attestation (AGENTS.md + MCP)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787080938893507001,"uuid":"74da5eec-c8a6-49f2-831c-31968d7f75a4"}